    "SCORES" : {

    },
    "Scores Effort on an exponential intensity curve (Banister TRIMP) instead of the default heart-rate zones (Edwards). The default earns nothing below half of your heart-rate reserve, so an hour of lifting — where hard sets average out against the rests — can score close to zero. The exponential curve has no floor and weights short, hard efforts far more heavily. Re-scores your history, and both scales reach the same maximum. Off by default." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Scores Strain on an exponential intensity curve (Banister TRIMP) instead of the default heart-rate zones (Edwards). The default earns nothing below half of your heart-rate reserve, so an hour of lifting — where hard sets average out against the rests — can score close to zero. The exponential curve has no floor and weights short, hard efforts far more heavily. Re-scores your history, and both scales reach the same maximum. Off by default."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Scores still calibrating, no single day-owner yet" : {

    },
    "Scores Strain on an exponential intensity curve (Banister TRIMP) instead of the default heart-rate zones (Edwards). The default earns nothing below half of your heart-rate reserve, so an hour of lifting — where hard sets average out against the rests — can score close to zero. The exponential curve has no floor and weights short, hard efforts far more heavily. Re-scores your history, and both scales reach the same maximum. Off by default." : {

