    },
    "Sends experimental protocol queries and records replies in the strap log. Also enables the experimental 5/MG strap alarm." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sends experimental protocol queries and records replies in the strap log. Also enables the experimental 5/MG WHOOP alarm."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sends the official app’s SetNotification mask (1c 01 ff) instead of NOOP’s 3f at the next connect. The ring packs ~10 packets per notification for the official app and one for NOOP (9× slower drains); this is the first candidate switch. Off by default; the next connect after turning it off is back on 3f. Watch the strap log for “-> notify_all(ff)” and compare notification sizes in the raw capture." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sends the official app’s SetNotification mask (1c 01 ff) instead of Sfz Health’s 3f at the next connect. The ring packs ~10 packets per notification for the official app and one for Sfz Health (9× slower drains); this is the first candidate switch. Off by default; the next connect after turning it off is back on 3f. Watch the strap log for “-> notify_all(ff)” and compare notification sizes in the raw capture."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sends the official app’s SetNotification mask (1c 01 ff) instead of Sfz Health’s 3f at the next connect. The ring packs ~10 packets per notification for the official app and one for Sfz Health (9× slower drains); this is the first candidate switch. Off by default; the next connect after turning it off is back on 3f. Watch the strap log for “-> notify_all(ff)” and compare notification sizes in the raw capture." : {

    },
    "Sends the read-only GET_BODY_LOCATION_AND_STATUS (0x54) and shows the strap's full raw reply, decoding the body-location record (revision / location / confidence / status) on WHOOP 4.0. Nothing is written to the strap, and it never changes wear detection or scoring." : {
