    },
    "The WHOOP keeps banking data on its own, so nothing is lost — Sfz Health just talks to it less often to help it last until you can charge it." : {

    },
    "The WHOOP keeps reporting a different time than Sfz Health sends, so its firmware alarm won't fire at your wake time — usually a WHOOP whose clock or alarm has reset. Reset the WHOOP in the official WHOOP app (or fully charge it and reconnect), and keep your phone's Clock alarm as your wake until it takes." : {

    },
    "The WHOOP MG has ECG electrodes in its clasp. This unlocks a gated, hand-run probe on the Devices screen that asks the strap to start its ECG subsystem and logs whatever comes back. MG only — a plain WHOOP 5.0 has no electrodes, and NOOP will refuse to send unless your strap identifies itself as an MG. Nobody has confirmed a strap honours these commands, so it may simply do nothing. Turn on “Record puffin frames to a file” below first if you want a complete byte-level capture to share." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The WHOOP MG has ECG electrodes in its clasp. This unlocks a gated, hand-run probe on the Devices screen that asks the WHOOP to start its ECG subsystem and logs whatever comes back. MG only — a plain WHOOP 5.0 has no electrodes, and Sfz Health will refuse to send unless your WHOOP identifies itself as an MG. Nobody has confirmed a WHOOP honours these commands, so it may simply do nothing. Turn on “Record puffin frames to a file” below first if you want a complete byte-level capture to share."
          }
        }
      }
    },
