    "Your numbers, your WHOOP, and how Sfz Health works. All on %@." : {

    },
    "Your Oura ring only measures daytime heart rate while NOOP keeps it in that mode, and NOOP stops asking whenever the screen has been off for five minutes — which protects the ring's own sleep tracking at night, but also leaves a pocketed phone's day blank on the Heart Rate and HRV charts. On, NOOP keeps asking through the day and stops only for your usual night, learned from your sleep history (an hour before your typical bedtime to an hour after your usual wake), so the night is unchanged. Costs ring battery: the ring runs its own optical sensor all day. Until enough nights are learned it behaves as if off. Off by default." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Oura ring only measures daytime heart rate while Sfz Health keeps it in that mode, and Sfz Health stops asking whenever the screen has been off for five minutes — which protects the ring's own sleep tracking at night, but also leaves a pocketed phone's day blank on the Heart Rate and HRV charts. On, Sfz Health keeps asking through the day and stops only for your usual night, learned from your sleep history (an hour before your typical bedtime to an hour after your usual wake), so the night is unchanged. Costs ring battery: the ring runs its own optical sensor all day. Until enough nights are learned it behaves as if off. Off by default."
          }
        }
      }
    },
